      "value": [
        {
          "resource_id": "levelled_description",
          "stats": {
            "id": "levelled_description_114ea33e9f30",
            "level": {
              "value": 10
            },
            "description": {
              "value": "Even if vitrumancy is a mystery to you, your blood and flesh know the secrets of the art of arcane glass. Patches of your skin to flicker into glass without warning. By focusing the effect, you can concentrate the glass into a powerful protective layer of magical obsidian. Once per day, you can cast stoneskin on yourself as an innate primal spell, though the spell covers you in a layer of glass instead of stone.\n\nDuring this innate stoneskin, you gain the Shatter Glass reaction."
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "levelled_description",
          "stats": {
            "id": "levelled_description_9691ee14d33e",
            "level": {
              "value": 14
            },
            "description": {
              "value": "The damage increases to 4d10"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "levelled_description",
          "stats": {
            "id": "levelled_description_0fac54452521",
            "level": {
              "value": 18
            },
            "description": {
              "value": "The stoneskin is heightened to 6th level instead of 4th.\n\n**Shatter Glass**\n\n- **Activate:** Reaction\n- **Trigger:** An adjacent creature Strikes you with a melee weapon or unarmed attack and deals damage\n- **Requirements:** Your innate stoneskin from Glass Skin is active\n\nYou shatter some of the glass on your skin to damage your attacker. The attacker takes 3d10 damage and the duration of the stoneskin decreases by 1 minute. The damage increases to 5d10."
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
